    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sd",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sc",
          "text": "Many drivers fail to recognize and respect bicyclists’ rights to the road. They may drive or pass too closely to bicycles, for example, or engage in other behaviors that put bicyclists at risk. If a driver in Colorado caused your bicycle accident, he or she may be financially responsible for your losses.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sf",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6se",
          "text": "What Are Your Rights as a Bicyclist in Colorado?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sh",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sg",
          "text": "Knowing your rights as a bicyclist in Colorado can help you avoid an accident. It will allow you to understand the traffic laws that apply to you and how to keep yourself safe from collisions with motor vehicles. If it is too late and you’ve already been injured in a bicycle accident in Thornton, learning your rights can help you build an injury claim against the driver who struck you. Some of the key rights given to bicyclists in Colorado are:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sk",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6si",
          "text": "Right to the road",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sj",
          "text": ". Many drivers mistakenly believe that bicyclists should ride on the sidewalk, not the road, when the opposite is actually true. Cyclists in Colorado have the same right to use the road as motor vehicle drivers. In fact, many municipalities make bike riding on the sidewalk illegal.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sn",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sl",
          "text": "Right to space",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sm",
          "text": ". Motorists must leave at least three feet of space between their vehicles and bicycles when passing them on the road. They should also leave ample space when following behind bicyclists.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6so",
          "text": "Right to be free from harassment",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sp",
          "text": ". Even if a bicyclist cannot keep up with the speed of surrounding traffic, drivers behind the cyclist must be patient and respect the biker’s rights. Harassing, shouting or throwing things at a biker is against the law.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ss",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sr",
          "text": "If a motor vehicle driver infringed upon any of your rights as a bicyclist and this caused or significantly contributed to your accident, you may be able to use this as evidence against the driver to recover financial compensation from his or her insurance company. An in-depth review of your case by an attorney at Dormer Harpring, LLC can help you understand if you have a case against a driver – and if so, how much your case is worth.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6su",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6st",
          "text": "Compensation for a Bicycle Accident in Thornton",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6sz",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l6sw",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/thornton-personal-injury-attorney/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sv",
          "text": "Filing a bicycle accident claim with help from an attorney in Thornton could result in financial compensation for both economic and noneconomic losses. You may be eligible for compensation for your medical bills, lost wages, bicycle repairs, physical pain and suffering, emotional distress, and more. Our ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sx",
          "text": "injury attorneys in Thornton",
          "marks": [
            "l6sw"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6sy",
          "text": " can give you an accurate evaluation of your case during a case review.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t1",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t0",
          "text": "How to Prove Fault After a Bicycle Accident in Thornton",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t3",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t2",
          "text": "Before you can obtain financial compensation for a bicycle accident in Colorado, you or your attorney must prove that the driver (or another party) is at fault. This is the rule under Colorado’s fault-based insurance system. Proving fault requires a preponderance of the evidence – enough evidence to establish that the defendant is more likely to be responsible for your bicycle accident than not.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t5",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t4",
          "text": "A lawyer can help you gather evidence to support your bicycle accident claim from the very beginning. Evidence may include a police report, signed eyewitness statements, photographs, video surveillance footage, medical records and bicycle accident expert testimony. Then, your lawyer can help you present this evidence in a compelling way to maximize your chances of a successful settlement.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t7",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t6",
          "text": "Bicycle Accident Resources in Thornton, Colorado",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6t9",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6t8",
          "text": "Being involved in a bicycle accident can leave you with a lot of questions and confusion about what steps to take next. Luckily, there are resources available to help you. One is the attorneys at Dormer Harpring, LLC. During your free consultation, you can tell your story and have your legal questions answered by an experienced and knowledgeable attorney.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
